**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. Adding an item, as a pure update over the kit's items (001 §P: `AddItem` is a semantic message; the S7.1 brief: pure updates for AddItem, an item's parameters are created from the generated axes; 001 §I 'Two LPs of one model are two items with independent parameters'). In `Kit.fs`, after `Item` (step 215), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1. (1) `ItemModelChoice` = `SourcePresetChoice of model : ItemModelVersion * source : SourcePreset` | `PolarizerPresetChoice of model : ItemModelVersion * polarizer : PolarizerPreset` | `StackSampleChoice of model : ItemModelVersion * version : SampleVersionId * sample : Sample` | `LibraryModelChoice of ItemModelVersion`: a model as the library resolved it. `member this.instance : ItemModelInstance` MUST carry the choice's exact model version in every case: PresetInstance (model.versionId, preset.id), SampleInstance (model.versionId, version), or ItemModelVersionInstance model.versionId; `member this.parameterAxes : ItemParameterAxis list` MUST match the model form and typed binding, calling the preset/sample parameterAxes members (step 207) for SourcePresetItemModel, IdealPolarizerItemModel and StackSampleItemModel, or entry.model.parameterAxes for a standalone form (step 208). (2) `ItemDraft = { id : ItemId; label : ItemLabel; model : ItemModelChoice; dial : ItemDial }`, what `AddItem` gives. `member this.toItem : Item` holds the draft's id, label, `model.instance` and dial; its `parameters` are `Parameter.knownAtDefault` (step 214) of `model.parameterAxes` followed by `dial.parameterAxes`, in that order; `photoOpt = None`, `notes = ItemNotes ""`, `revision = ItemRevision.first` and `history = []`. `member this.addTo (items : Item list) : Result<Item, ItemError>` answers `DuplicateItemIdErr` when an item holds the id, `DuplicateItemLabelErr` naming both labels when an item's label `fileStem` equals the draft's ignoring case (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`), because every `<label>.item-json` shares the kit root on Windows, and MUST validate that each resolved model has the form matching its binding before returning toItem. An absent/mismatched model, a non-GUID preset binding or LibraryModelChoice of an unbound binding-required form MUST yield InvalidItemModelBindingErr before an item is recorded. It writes nothing; the caller records the item (step 219). Every source, ideal-polarizer and sample test draft MUST receive the corresponding BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel from step 210. The declared source/polarizer/sample fact MUST assert a model version in every item and exercise the mismatched-model refusal without changing the kit. No other member, option or default is added. Tests, in `KitItemTests`: `adding an item from a library model creates its parameters known at the model's defaults and its dial zero`: a CPL1 item made by an `ItemDraft` over `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId)` and `DialMounted DialPositive` holds the parameters `c1.extinctionRatio`, `c1.axisOffset`, `c2.retardance`, `c2.fastAxisOffset` and `dialZero`, each `KnownParameter` of its axis default, its model `ItemModelVersionInstance` of that model's `versionId`, revision 1, no history, no photo and empty notes. `a source preset, an ideal polarizer and a sample give an item their own parameters`: a `SourcePresetChoice` of `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633` with `FixedMounting` holds `azimuth`, `ellipticity`, `degreeOfPolarization` and `intensityScale`; a `PolarizerPresetChoice` of the `PresetIds.polarizerLp` polarizer with `DialMounted DialNegative` holds `dialZero` alone; a `StackSampleChoice` of `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1 with its catalogue sample holds `substrate.thickness` at 1e-3 and the `SampleInstance` of the stack item-model version and that sample version. `two items of one model are two items with equal starting parameters`: LP1 and LP2, two drafts over the `ItemModelIds.realLinearPolarizerModelId` model with distinct test-local ids, are two items whose parameters are equal and whose ids and labels differ. `adding an item whose id or label file name the kit already holds is refused`: over a kit holding LP1, a draft labelled `lp1`, and one labelled `LP:1` beside an item labelled `LP_1`, answer `DuplicateItemLabelErr`, and a draft reusing LP1's id answers `DuplicateItemIdErr`.

**Acceptance.** After AddItem lands, `ItemDraft.toItem` MUST create every parameter its model and dial publish, known at its default, at revision 1, and `ItemDraft.addTo` MUST refuse an id or a label file name the kit already holds; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `adding an item from a library model creates its parameters known at the model's defaults and its dial zero`, `a source preset, an ideal polarizer and a sample give an item their own parameters`, `two items of one model are two items with equal starting parameters` and `adding an item whose id or label file name the kit already holds is refused`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass. Every item MUST carry an exact ItemModel version, with source/polarizer/sample references treated only as typed physics dependencies; no direct-preset or direct-sample model bypass is permitted.
